  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "RNA-only PCA singleprofile is currently the strongest result (0.485 accuracy, 0.464 F1), while image-only ResNet is much weaker (0.208 accuracy, 0.172 F1), suggesting RNA is the more promising direction. The key uncertainty is whether the PCA representation is already adequate or whether a learned RNA encoder can improve performance. config_004 tests this directly by changing only the RNA encoder from PCA to SCVI n200 while keeping singleprofile and avoiding image, fusion, or multiprofile complexity. This is a simple, high-information extension of the best baseline and is a better use of limited budget than jumping to more complex multimodal or multiprofile settings."
}

